774d5e7198d moved POST /api/sessions/{id}/mute, GET /outcome?refresh=1 and owner-backfill onto the
live owner's store, but only when the gateway runner is composed into the same app. Desktop on a
remote host (hermes-hub) talks to an SSH-isolated `serve` with no runner, which still took the
offline maintenance lock and 409'd ('Exclusive maintenance refused'; hub gui.log at 05:35 and 09:40
after that fix deployed). Such a backend now replays the write on the owner's own HTTP API with a
single-use native-http ticket minted on its control socket. Live-gateway test with an uncomposed
app (RED = the exact 409).
